		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 296ca8b8-3710-4726-b4d5-397a74fc5a36</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Testing</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Testing involves sending the 'is_ok()' message to the modules and then reading the returned value. If the value is not returned within the specified time, the test is considered failed.</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:22:30</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 065ef9f8-fa42-441e-9e67-ef590a5d12f6</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Stopping</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Stopping%0D
%0D
Stopping the gate may result from reaching one of the end positions or the occurrence of a collision.%0D
The procedure should in order:%0D
%0D
1. Switch off the drive%0D
2. Turn off the collision detector%0D
3. Optionally, turn off the signal lamp</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::15:45:34</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 2e0beab1-2e1e-4e7d-a0ba-c4302d177b99</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">State indication</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">State indication%0D
%0D
Optionally the lamp will be blinking, possibly with different rate in case of opening and closing the gate.</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::15:44:16</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
