		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 2df6ec98-4bc0-48da-932a-292046c66cb3</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Movement</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">The transition to the gate movement in the given direction requires the following steps:%0D
1. Turn on the collision detection%0D
2. Optional activation of the signaling lamp.%0D
3. Turning on the gate drive%0D
During the movement taking place in a given direction, the following actions should be repeated every fixed period of time.%0D
1. Send a signal about the last travelled distance to the Controller%0D
2. Check the occurence of a collision and if the collision detector signals it, stop the gate movement.%0D
3. If the signaling option is active, flash the lamp.</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::15:40:30</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID b070a96c-d26e-4e99-9bbd-b2852f4f1dd1</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Firmware</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Firmware updates</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::10:20:59</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 32090fb6-69e4-4dd6-a0d2-abf32e520799</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Collision detection</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Collision detection should take place in each period (iteration) of the gate movement and consists in counting by the infrared receiver the pulses sent by the infrared trasmitter.%0D
1. If the number of pulses received and sent differ significantly, send an appropriate signal to the Controller, which should stop the drive.%0D
2. Otherwise, keep moving.%0D
</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::15:43:37</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID ba896025-80de-4307-a6ca-3645026a7a68</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Authentication</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_text type="a">Authentication consists of entering 4 digits and comparing them with the password%0D
</_text>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::15:52:55</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
